%% Converting spike times to NREM binary spike trains
% This script loads the spike-time matrix for all recorded cells from the
% Mouse12-120808 experiment and defines the predefined NREM/SWS episodes.
%
% The NREM/SWS intervals are converted into a logical sample index based
% on the 1250 Hz EEG sampling frequency. Each spike time is then mapped to
% the nearest sample of the complete EEG time vector and represented as a
% binary spike train.
%
% The spike trains are restricted to the NREM/SWS periods, producing a
% matrix in which each row represents one cell and each column represents
% an EEG sample during NREM. The resulting NREM spike-train matrix is
% saved as a MAT file for subsequent neuronal activity analysis.

clear 
close all

% load Mouse12-120806.spikes.cellinfo.mat
load    SpikesTimesAllCells.mat
%SWS times Episode 
SwsTime = [456.47	586.1
